+- **A Codex install could not run the sprint loop: Codex's default `workspace-write` sandbox kept
+  `.git` read-only, so the first commit failed (BUG-100).** Inside a git repository,
+  `cleargate init --host codex` and `cleargate host add codex` now add the realpath of
+  `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` (the main `.git`, which also covers every linked worktree) to
+  `[sandbox_workspace_write] writable_roots` in `.codex/config.toml`, and print one line naming that
+  absolute path. Other roots are kept; on re-init an absolute `.git` root that no longer exists is
+  replaced. `cleargate uninstall` and `cleargate host remove codex` remove only ClearGate's root. A
+  non-git install writes no key, and an inline-table or dotted-key definition is refused before any
+  write unless it already holds the root. `cleargate upgrade` does not refresh the key yet.
+- **An item edited after its last gate check stayed `stale` forever (BUG-047).** `cleargate stamp`
+  moves `updated_at` past `last_gate_check`, but `gate check` skipped the write whenever the verdict
+  was unchanged, and `sprint preflight` Step 0 reverted any timestamp-only rewrite, so preflight
+  Check 5 and `wiki lint` kept reporting the item stale and the suggested `gate check` could not
+  clear it. A single freshness rule (`isGateCacheFresh`: `last_gate_check >= updated_at`) now
+  decides both: `gate check` rewrites a stale cache even for an unchanged verdict, Step 0 keeps a
+  stale item's advanced stamp, and an already-fresh item is still left byte-identical (CR-038).
+  Check 5 uses the same rule for items and the sprint plan; a cache with no `last_gate_check` now
+  counts as stale.
